@base = http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/booking
@floor = 40000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@room = 50000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@user = 60000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

### Company and its domains
GET {{base}}/CompanyDomains?$filter=domain eq 'example.com'&$expand=company

### Geographic hierarchy
GET {{base}}/Sites?$expand=buildings($expand=floors)&$orderby=city

### Resources and location
GET {{base}}/Resources?$expand=floor($expand=building($expand=site))

### Rooms and workplaces are read-only views
GET {{base}}/Rooms

### Workplaces
GET {{base}}/Workplaces

### Create a room; code must be unique within its floor
POST {{base}}/Resources
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "floor_ID": "{{floor}}",
  "type": "ROOM",
  "code": "H-A-1-WORKSHOP",
  "name": "Workshop",
  "capacity": 12,
  "roomType": "MEETING"
}

### Create a workplace
POST {{base}}/Resources
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "floor_ID": "{{floor}}",
  "type": "WORKPLACE",
  "code": "H-A-1-DESK-NEW",
  "name": "Window desk",
  "workplaceType": "HOT_DESK",
  "monitorCount": 2
}

### Create a booking; repeating this request returns 409
# @name createdBooking
POST {{base}}/Bookings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "resource_ID": "{{room}}",
  "user_ID": "{{user}}",
  "title": "Project planning",
  "startAt": "2026-09-15T09:00:00+02:00",
  "endAt": "2026-09-15T10:00:00+02:00",
  "attendeeCount": 4
}

### Read bookings
GET {{base}}/Bookings?$expand=resource,user&$orderby=startAt

### Cancel the booking (VS Code REST Client response variable)
PATCH {{base}}/Bookings({{createdBooking.response.body.$.ID}})
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "CANCELLED"
}

### Reference opening hours
GET {{base}}/OpeningHours?$expand=site&$orderby=dayOfWeek
